From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brad Nicholas <70774+bradn@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 09:02:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Comment the width patch against upstream's original
 behaviour

Each change now says what v1.0.16 did and why it changed: the four
68-72 clamps (stylesheet, container, profiles, Settings stepper), the
container forcing 72 above 1200pt, Quick Look ignoring the measure, the
checkbox sample clamp, and install.sh's undefined STAGED_APP. Comments
only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
Authored by Claude Code as directed by Brad Nicholas <70774+bradn@users.noreply.github.com>
 Scripts/install.sh                                     |  3 +++
 .../DownrightApp/App/PreferencesWindowController.swift |  3 +++
 .../DownrightApp/Panels/ReaderProfilePickerView.swift  |  5 +++--
 Sources/DownrightApp/Support/Preferences.swift         |  2 ++
 Sources/DownrightApp/Support/ReaderProfiles.swift      |  2 ++
 Sources/DownrightQL/PreviewViewController.swift        |  4 ++++
 Sources/MarkdownRender/Theme/PreviewAppearance.swift   |  2 ++
 Sources/MarkdownRender/Theme/StyleSheet.swift          |  3 +++
 .../MarkdownRender/View/MarkdownContainerView.swift    | 10 +++++++---
 .../View/MarkdownTextView+Interaction.swift            |  7 +++++--
 10 files changed, 34 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Scripts/install.sh b/Scripts/install.sh
index 53b7211..6576027 100755
--- a/Scripts/install.sh
+++ b/Scripts/install.sh
@@ -35,6 +35,9 @@ fi
 echo "==> Installing to $APP_DEST"
 DEST_PARENT="$(dirname "$APP_DEST")"
 STAGE_ROOT="$(mktemp -d "$DEST_PARENT/.downright-install.XXXXXX")"
+# Local fix (width patch): upstream v1.0.16 uses STAGED_APP below but never
+# defines it, so under `set -u` the install aborted at the copy step with
+# "unbound variable" before touching /Applications.
 STAGED_APP="$STAGE_ROOT/Downright.app"
 # The backup of the outgoing app deliberately lives OUTSIDE the staging tree
 # the exit trap deletes. Between "old app moved aside" and "new app in
diff --git a/Sources/DownrightApp/App/PreferencesWindowController.swift b/Sources/DownrightApp/App/PreferencesWindowController.swift
index aadba25..0cc966b 100644
--- a/Sources/DownrightApp/App/PreferencesWindowController.swift
+++ b/Sources/DownrightApp/App/PreferencesWindowController.swift
@@ -887,6 +887,9 @@ enum PreferencesForms {
             .stepper("Line height", help: nil, range: 1.2...2.0, step: 0.05,
                      get: { Double(Preferences.shared.values.typography.lineHeightMultiple) },
                      set: { value in Preferences.shared.update { $0.typography.lineHeightMultiple = CGFloat(value) } }),
+            // Upstream offered 60...80 here, though the renderer clamped to
+            // 68–72, so 60–67 and 73–80 silently did nothing.  The stepper now
+            // spans exactly what the renderer honours (width patch).
             .stepper("Measure (characters)",
                      help: "How much text fits on a line before it wraps. Around 68 to 72 reads best. Larger values widen the column up to the window width.",
                      range: Double(ReadingMeasure.minimumCharacters)...Double(ReadingMeasure.maximumCharacters), step: 1,
